            <ArticleTitle>Open cardiac operations in patients with abnormalities of white blood cell number or function.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1065-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abnormality of white blood cell number or function has been viewed by some as a relative contraindication to operations done with cardiopulmonary bypass. We have operated upon three patients, each with a different white blood cell abnormality, with good results. We do not believe these patients should be denied operation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
